# Every text file in this repository is LF in the working tree, on every
# platform. This is not a style preference; two things break without it.
#
# gofmt insists on LF, so a Windows checkout under git's default
# core.autocrlf=true reports every .go file as unformatted. That is exactly what
# the first CI run on windows-latest did.
#
# A behavior case embeds its script inside a TOML multi-line string, so the
# file's line endings become the script's. Nemosh normalizes CRLF and dash
# treats a lone CR as data, which means one fixture describes different
# behaviour depending on how it was checked out. The differential runner did
# catch that, and reported it as a difference between shells rather than as the
# artifact it was.
#
# text=auto still uses content detection, so anything genuinely binary is left
# alone. No .bat or .cmd files are tracked here; if any are added they want
# eol=crlf, because cmd.exe is particular about it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.go text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.sum text eol=lf
